[auto_map_race_node-10] facing the racing direction (the way it drove while mapping). The
[auto_map_race_node-10] race launch finds it from its LiDAR and refuses, saying why, if it
[auto_map_race_node-10] cannot: the map may be wrong, the place may look like another part
[auto_map_race_node-10] of the course, or the car may be facing backwards.
[auto_map_race_node-10] Use start:=start_pose to start exactly where mapping stopped instead.
